# No Alyx from cluster jobs

Incident 2026-11-02: per-insertion `load_trials_and_mask` calls in remote-mode
ONE sent ~120k requests from ~200 concurrent shards and throttled Alyx for
other IBL users.

- Build ONE with `make_one()` from `one_offline.py`, never `ONE()` directly.
  Inside Slurm it is offline and HTTP to `*.internationalbrainlab.org` raises
  `AlyxBlockedError`. Do not set `ALLOW_ALYX_IN_SLURM` or `ONE_MODE=remote`
  for a fan-out job.
- Loops must not swallow offline data errors (`is_missing_local_data`):
  a missing file is a stop, not a skipped insertion.
- Code a shard runs per insertion or per split reads disk only: the insertion
  cache, `bwm_tables/*.pqt`, memoized tables. Never call `download_*`,
  `pid2eid`, `one.search`, `one.alyx.*` there.
- Before printing a submit command, `scripts/check_offline_inputs.py` must
  pass (submit wrappers run it; `PREFLIGHT=0` only when the user says so).
- Before pushing code that cluster jobs run, run one real insertion with
  `SLURM_JOB_ID=test` (Alyx blocked) through the changed path, and state
  "Alyx requests per job × jobs" in the summary. Nonzero is a stop.
